From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: musa <musa@local>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:40:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] MUSA: fix Qwen4Exp Triton 3.2 compatibility

Three Triton 3.2 differences break the Qwen4Exp kernels on MUSA:

- the PLE lookup kernel annotates its byte pointers with tl.pointer_type,
  which the 3.2 signature parser mangles into "u8>" and rejects with
  KeyError, so cast in the body instead;
- Triton 3.2 has no tl.gather, and it compiles both arms of a
  "constexpr and tensor" condition, so the QSA metadata kernel needs a
  serial gather helper plus a nested constexpr guard for a null work
  pointer;
- max() inside a jit body resolves to tl.maximum, which drops the
  constexpr type tl.arange needs for the indexer block size.

The indexer also dispatched to vLLM's CUDA-only persistent_topk, so this
selects blocks with torch.topk until the MUSA radix-select kernel lands.
